    "compose_patient": {
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You were in a road traffic collision. You were hurt in several ways:\n\n- A broken bone in your left lower leg (left tibial shaft fracture)\n- A small tear in your spleen (grade II splenic laceration)\n- Broken ribs on your left side (ribs 7 to 9) with some blood collecting around your lung (haemothorax)\n- Small fractures in a bone in your lower back (L1 transverse process fractures)"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "Several teams looked after you: orthopaedics, general surgery, and the chest team.\n\nFor your leg, surgeons fixed the broken bone with a metal rod on 13/05.\n\nFor your ribs and lung, a drain was put into your chest to remove the blood. Your lung re-expanded well. The drain was taken out on 15/05. A chest X-ray on 15/05 looked satisfactory.\n\nFor your spleen, the team watched it carefully with regular checks and blood tests. No operation was needed. A scan on 15/05 showed it was improving and your blood levels stayed stable.\n\nThe team also gave you injections to help prevent blood clots while you were in hospital.\n\nA physiotherapist helped you start moving and walking, putting some weight on your left leg."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7"
          ],
          "text": "You have two follow-up appointments to come:\n\n- Orthopaedic fracture clinic in 2 weeks, about your leg.\n- General surgery telephone review at 6 weeks, about your spleen. The team will give you advice about a vaccination for your spleen at that call.\n\nThe chest team do not need to see you again routinely."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
